# `D-80`. Both `infra/deploy/Dockerfile.api` and `Dockerfile.web` build with
# `context: ../..` (`infra/deploy/compose.server.yml`), so without this file every build
# ships the WHOLE repository working tree to the docker daemon, including directories
# no COPY instruction ever names.
#
# Two distinct costs, both measured on a real build rather than assumed:
#
# 1. SIZE. The build context is transferred before either Dockerfile is even read, so
#    everything below is sent and hashed whether or not any COPY reaches it. Measured
#    at `1664f90` in a working tree with `.local/`, `.venv/` and `web/node_modules/`
#    populated: 563.89 MB transferred to build the web image alone, dominated by
#    `web/node_modules` (576 MB on disk) and this session's own `.local/` (219 MB of
#    uv/pip cache from `make bootstrap` -- a *different* `.local/` than the 5.3 GB norms
#    corpus the row was originally measured against in the main checkout, and both are
#    swept in by the same unbounded context for the same reason).
#
# 2. CORRECTNESS. `Dockerfile.web` runs `npm ci` against the lockfile and THEN
#    `COPY web/ ./`, which OVERLAYS the build host's `web/node_modules` on top of the
#    clean install -- `COPY` merges, it does not replace. Proved on this host: a marker
#    file planted only in the host's `web/node_modules` (never produced by `npm ci`)
#    was present in `/web/node_modules/` of the image built without this file, and
#    absent once this file excluded `**/node_modules` from the context. Without this
#    exclusion, `package-lock.json`, `pinned-versions.guard.test.ts` and
#    `web/FRONTEND_LOCK.json` describe a tree the image need not actually contain.
#
# Correction to the row as measured: under this host's BuildKit (docker 29.8, the
# default builder), the API build was never 6+ GB on its own -- its COPY instructions
# name specific paths (`src/`, `db/`, `contracts/`, `fixtures/recorded/`, ...) and
# BuildKit only requests what a COPY names, so its context stayed a few kB either way
# (measured: 16.30 kB, identical with and without this file). The size defect is
# `Dockerfile.web`'s alone, because `COPY web/ ./` names a whole subtree rather than
# individual paths. This file is still correct for both images -- it is what makes the
# node_modules overlay impossible for `web` and is cheap insurance for `api` -- the
# correction is about which build the SIZE half of this row actually costs.
#
# A clean clone has none of the directories below, which is exactly why `PA-01`
# criterion 1 (deploy from a clean clone) cannot see this defect -- `D-80`.
#
# Verified by a real build of both images after this file was added, not by inspection:
# a `.dockerignore` line that excludes something a `COPY` instruction names by path
# would fail the build outright, and changing what `COPY web/ ./` sees is this file's
# whole purpose.

.git
.local
.venv
**/node_modules
web/.next
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
